// Polish chapter state: the state tree S of the technical reference (2.4), created by the rules
// module (source/rules/polish_rules.js). The seed reads the generator state without drawing from it.
// The parliament, Senate and ballot domains start from the opening Sejm (polish_institutions.js);
// actors, agreements and the opening cabinet from the relations and cabinet above
// (polish_government.js); the economy and society from economy_simple_v1 (polish_economy.js).
Q.S = PolishRules.createFoundationState({randomState: this.random.getState(),
    institutions: PolishInstitutions.createInstitutionState(Q),
    government: PolishGovernment.createGovernmentState(Q),
    economy: PolishEconomy.createEconomyState()});
PolishGovernment.writeRelationMirrors(Q);
// The Polish economy (stage 4) owns budget, prices, wages, output, credit and unemployment; the
// inherited fields are mirrors written from S.economy, and the German monthly economy is off.
Q.polish_economy_system = 1;
PolishEconomy.writeEconomyMirrors(Q);
// The party of stage 5 (implementation plan, decision 1A): disjoint cells of the electorate own the
// preferences, built so that today's national result of the opening stays exactly the same; the class
// rows become their mirrors. Party money, organisations, Milicja, the union branches and the factions have
// their owner in Q.S; the inherited fields are mirrors (technical reference 5.1–5.2, 10.1, 13, 14.1).
PolishElectorate.seedCells(Q);
PolishElectorate.writeClassMirrors(Q);
PolishParty.attachPartyState(Q);
Q.polish_party_rules = 1;
// Stage 6: unions and strikes (technical reference 14.1–14.5): the branches get the lines of a strike call, and the
// records of strikes and plants start empty.
PolishUnions.attachUnionState(Q);
Q.polish_union_rules = 1;
// Stage 7: politics and society (technical reference 15.1–15.3): the journal of institutions, democracy, violence,
// the grievance of the cells and the pressure towards a coup.
PolishPolitics.attachPoliticsState(Q);
Q.polish_politics_rules = 1;
// Stage 7: the forces of the state (technical reference 16.1–16.3, 16.7): the synthetic army groups, the police, the
// uncertain assessment of their loyalty and the agreement with Piłsudski.
PolishSecurity.attachSecurityState(Q);
Q.polish_security_rules = 1;
!}
new-page: true

= Poland, January 1922

Józef Piłsudski is **Naczelnik Państwa**, not President of the Republic. **Antoni Ponikowski** leads a predominantly expert cabinet. The **Sejm Ustawodawczy** remains the legislature under the transitional arrangements accompanying the March Constitution; there is no operating Senate or presidential officeholder at the opening.

**We tolerate Ponikowski's government, but we are outside the cabinet and control no ministries.** Campaigning, party organization, advisers and Milicja PPS remain available under their existing rules. Toleration does not grant command of the state police or executive powers.

The opening uses an approved **444-MP gameplay approximation**, calculated from rounded August 1922 club shares, not an exact January roster. Parliamentary representation is separate from changing public support.

Read the Library for the opening institutions and cabinet portfolios. **The first Sejm election is in November 1922: 444 MPs, with 223 needed for a majority.** The cabinet that follows is negotiated in the same sequence and consumes no extra monthly action. In December, the new Sejm elects its Marshal and the National Assembly elects the President without another action; the clubs' votes decide both offices. The chapter ends with a report: when an attempted coup is resolved, or with the certified result of the next lawful Sejm election, on 19 February 1928 in the game's legal calendar.

